# Agent workflow (token-efficient)

## Checkout before explore

For PR work (`/thermos`, review fixes), **fetch and checkout the PR head branch first**. Do not grep or read production code on `main` when a PR branch exists.

## No duplicate work

- **`/thermos`:** one invocation runs the full pipeline in `thermo-nuclear-review` (deterministic scan → blind audit → fix → **closure pass** → SHIP). Do not ask for a second session for a fresh look — closure pass is the second check.
- **Cloud Agent self-verification:** **commit implementation** on the feature branch first
  (thermo diffs use `origin/<base>...HEAD`). Then run Gradle verify when Kotlin/plugin code
  changed, then `thermo-nuclear-review` Phases 1–5 **before** the final push that opens or
  updates the PR. Fix P0–P2 on branch; file or fix every P3; closure pass is mandatory.
  Gradle passing alone is not sufficient to skip thermo.
- **Resume** IDLE sessions only for continuations (push, issue comment, PR polish) — not to skip Thermo phases on a new `/thermos` request or a new implementation verification.
- Push-only / link-only follow-ups: create issues or push — **do not** re-run audit or tests.

## Gradle test tasks

Modules use the JVM Test Suite plugin (`testing { suites { … } }` in `build-logic`). Configure test tasks via `getByName<JvmTestSuite>("test") { targets.all { testTask.configure { … } } }`.

**Do not** add bare `tasks.named<Test>("test") { … }` when the module already has `testing { suites }`. Pattern: `build-logic/src/main/kotlin/com.linecorp.intellij.platform-library.gradle.kts`.

## Skill routing

Read `workflow-router` first for `/thermos`, PR comment triage, issue fixes, or Cloud Agent post-implementation verification — then only the matching on-demand skill (`thermo-nuclear-review`, `pr-review-response`, or `issue-to-pr`).
